  "before_command": "PYTHONPATH=src:. python scripts/benchmark_command_latency.py",
  "after_command": "PYTHONPATH=src python -m scripts.benchmark_command_latency --include-async-settings",
  "notes": [
    "Before was measured before changes to runtime or completion code; after uses the working-tree fix.",
    "Both runs use four callback workers, eight independent batches and a 20 ms per-frame sender delay.",
    "Command latency covers dispatch entry, construction, acceptance, encoding, setup gate, receipt and local commit.",
    "Input latency covers the typed inbound queue, pump and scheduler; JSON decoding and physical device I/O are excluded.",
    "Occupancy is sampled with the first send gated, before the input probe. Settings modes use one writer and three snapshot readers.",
    "Small synthetic samples demonstrate blocking; these p95/p99 values are not production tail-latency estimates.",
    "One async settings transaction is accepted at a time; busy rejections are explicit and are not queued."
  ],
